From: qin46xia
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: soe: hash decrypted packets by inner flow

airoha_soe_restore_metadata() copies the header of the original ESP skb,
including its flow hash. Every decrypted packet of an SA then carries the
same outer-flow hash and RPS steers all of them to one CPU, which caps
inbound IPsec at one core. Clear the hash before netif_rx() so RPS hashes
the inner flow.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
index 982c07f..eb7fece 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
@@ -3146,6 +3146,11 @@ static bool airoha_soe_complete_in(struct sk_buff *skb,
 
 	nf_reset_ct(skb);
 	kfree(ctx);
+	/* The header copied from the ESP skb carries the outer flow hash,
+	 * which is the same for every packet of the SA. Let RPS hash the
+	 * decrypted inner flow instead so tunnelled flows spread over CPUs.
+	 */
+	skb_clear_hash(skb);
 	netif_rx(skb);
 
 	return true;
